The '''International Brigades''' ([[Baliscano]]: ''Brigadas international;'' often abbreviated '''BI''') is a predominately [[W:Anarchism|anarchist]] armed organization, which effectively operated as [[W:Far-left|left-unity]] [[W:Paramilitary|paramilitary]] that engaged in direct medical and military internationalism in support of left-wing [[W:Revolutionary movement|revolutionary]] and [[W:Liberation movement|liberation movements]] worldwide, but never for governments. 

It has fought as a [[W:paramilitary|volunteer]] force in several revolutionary conflicts. It first saw action in the the [[Burawi Domestic War]] in support of [[tba]]. Balisca had relatively [[Balisca–Burawa relations|turbulent relations]] with the emerging administration of [[Maana Kadar]], but the two reconciled in order to collaborate against reactionary forces.

It was able to circumvent the confederal policy of non-aggression during the [[Abyalan Cold War]] following the [[Kuluba Accords]], bringing together various autonomous leftist factions within the Confederation united by their shared support of {{W|proletarian internationalism}}. The Brigades were largely viewed as defunct following the end of the Cold War.  

The Brigades' three-pointed Red Star is the emblem of unity of all progressive forces. It means the world-wide cooperation of Marxists, Anarchists and Republican Democrats. Sometimes this is expressed as the unity in principle of Marxists, Anarchists and Trade Unionists, depending upon context.  {{Balisca articles}}
